-- title:
--   Vanishing dichotomy on a fibre of a projective presentation
-- statement:
--   Let $k$ be an algebraically closed field, $X$ a scheme and $t\colon X\to\operatorname{Spec} k$ a proper morphism, and let $M$ be an object of `X.Modules` which is invertible in the sense of `Scheme.Modules.IsInvertible`: every point of $X$ has an open neighbourhood $U$ such that the pullback of $M$ along $U\hookrightarrow X$ is isomorphic to the unit sheaf of modules on $U$. Let $N$ be a natural number and let $\mathfrak P$ be a `ProjPresentation` of $M$ over $t$ of size $N$, that is: global sections $\sigma_i\in\Gamma(M,\top)$ for $i\in\mathrm{Fin}(N+1)$, a morphism $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{toProj}\colon X\to\operatorname{Proj}$ of the graded algebra of homogeneous polynomials in $N+1$ variables over $k$ whose composite with the structure morphism `ProjSpace.π` is $t$, such that for each $i$ and each open $V$ contained in the preimage of the basic open set $D_+(X_i)$ the map $g\mapsto g\cdot\sigma_i|_V$ from $\Gamma(X,V)$ to $\Gamma(M,V)$ is bijective, and such that on the preimage of $D_+(X_i)$ the pulled-back ratio $X_j/X_i$ carries $\sigma_i$ to $\sigma_j$. Let $Z\subseteq X$ be closed and irreducible, let $y$ be a point of $\operatorname{Proj}$ with $\{y\}$ closed and assume $Z$ is contained in the preimage of $\{y\}$ under the underlying map of $\mathfrak P.\mathrm{toProj}$. Then for every morphism $s$ from the unit module $\mathbf 1_{X.\mathrm{Modules}}$ to $M$, the set $Z$ is either contained in the support of the ideal sheaf data `zeroSchemeIdeal s` — the infimum of those ideal sheaf data $J$ with $\mathrm{coeffIdeal}(s,U)\le J(U)$ for every affine open $U$, where $\mathrm{coeffIdeal}(s,U)$ is generated by the coefficients of $s$ on $U$ — or disjoint from that support.
--
--   This is the dichotomy, in Mumford's treatment of rigidity-type arguments, that a global section of a line bundle either vanishes identically on a subvariety contracted to a point by the associated projective morphism, or vanishes nowhere on it. It feeds the finiteness criteria `isFinite_toProj_of_finite_setOf_forall_pullbackSection_eq_zero_iff` and `isFinite_toProj_of_forall_pullbackSection_eq_zero_iff` for the morphism to projective space attached to a presentation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/anthropics/fermats-last-theorem/blob/aa2d8b34692b16c70f699536de0d8e75b9a3e9ef/Theorems/Thm_AlgebraicGeometry_Scheme_Modules_ProjPresentation_subset_support_zeroSchemeIdeal_or_disjoint.lean

